; Draw a 16x16 sprite, optionally testing for collision
;
; Draws a 16x16 sprite of 16 pixel rows, 2 bytes per row (left byte, right byte;
; 32 bytes, row-interleaved), at a byte-aligned position in a Spectrum-layout
; bitmap. The target is either the screen ($4000) or a buffer in the same
; layout (the $6000 buffer, see #R$8200).
; .
; Mode 0 (C bit 0 clear): the sprite bytes replace the bitmap bytes.
; .
; Mode 1 (C bit 0 set): collision test. Each sprite byte is ANDed with the
; bitmap byte under it; if the result is not zero the routine returns at once
; with NZ (rows drawn before that stay drawn); otherwise the byte is ORed in.
; .
; The address steps down a pixel row with INC H and handles the character-row
; and one-third-of-the-bitmap boundaries.
; .
; Callers: #R$86C3, #R$898B and #R$8B07 use mode 0 directly on the screen
; (C = 0). #R$91BE and #R$9534 use mode 1 on the $6000 buffer, after Willy and
; the room are already drawn there, and send a collision to #R$90B7 (observed
; in the Bathroom: C = 1, DE = $B900, HL = $607B). Observed with a test call:
; mode 0 replaces bytes and returns Z with HL = $6040 after a sprite drawn at
; $6000; mode 1 over set pixels returns NZ with part of the sprite drawn.
; .
; Hardware: writes the screen bitmap or a bitmap buffer in screen layout.
;
; DE Sprite graphic address
; HL Bitmap address of the top-left byte
; C Bit 0: 0 = overwrite, 1 = draw with collision test
; O:A 0 when drawn completely (Z set); in mode 1, the overlapping bits when stopped (NZ)
; O:HL Bitmap address of the pixel row below the sprite (when drawn completely)
@label=DrawSprite
@isub=LD B,SPRITE_HEIGHT
c$9456 LD B,$10      ;
@label=DrawSprite_Row
*$9458 BIT 0,C       ;
 $945A LD A,(DE)     ;
 $945B JR Z,$9461    ;
 $945D AND (HL)      ;
 $945E RET NZ        ; collision with the left byte
 $945F LD A,(DE)     ;
 $9460 OR (HL)       ;
*$9461 LD (HL),A     ;
 $9462 INC L         ;
 $9463 INC DE        ;
 $9464 BIT 0,C       ;
 $9466 LD A,(DE)     ;
 $9467 JR Z,$946D    ;
 $9469 AND (HL)      ;
 $946A RET NZ        ; collision with the right byte
 $946B LD A,(DE)     ;
 $946C OR (HL)       ;
*$946D LD (HL),A     ;
 $946E DEC L         ;
 $946F INC H         ; next pixel row
 $9470 INC DE        ;
 $9471 LD A,H        ;
@isub=AND CELL_HEIGHT-1
 $9472 AND $07       ;
 $9474 JR NZ,$9486   ;
 $9476 LD A,H        ; crossed into the next character row
@isub=SUB CELL_HEIGHT
 $9477 SUB $08       ;
 $9479 LD H,A        ;
 $947A LD A,L        ;
@isub=ADD A,SCREEN_COLS
 $947B ADD A,$20     ;
 $947D LD L,A        ;
@isub=AND ~COLUMN_MASK
 $947E AND $E0       ;
 $9480 JR NZ,$9486   ;
 $9482 LD A,H        ; crossed into the next third of the bitmap
@isub=ADD A,THIRD_PAGES
 $9483 ADD A,$08     ;
 $9485 LD H,A        ;
*$9486 DJNZ $9458    ;
 $9488 XOR A         ; Z set: no collision
 $9489 RET           ;
